  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115812",
      "title": "Updating Signal Values",
      "lectureOrder": 144,
      "videoOrder": 136,
      "sourceHash": "e31e8f619da9a644243bc486d00dfda2852b8d707da27bd80ab35112c5f1fb99",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.81,
          "end": 3.06,
          "en": "So I now wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.06,
          "end": 4.62,
          "en": "that we can click this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.62,
          "end": 7.83,
          "en": "or actually here, this entire title should be a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.83,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "and we can click this to collapse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 13.44,
          "en": "or expand the ticket details.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.44,
          "end": 16.83,
          "en": "To do that, we can go to that ticket component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.83,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "TypeScript file again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "and in there we can add a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 24.873,
          "en": "that could be named details visible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.873,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "and we can either set it to false initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 31.65,
          "en": "or use signals for managing that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 36.01,
          "en": "by creating a signal that has an initial value of false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.01,
          "end": 39.09,
          "en": "or true, depending on whether the details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.09,
          "end": 41.25,
          "en": "should be visible initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.25,
          "end": 44.94,
          "en": "But I'll start with false as an initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.94,
          "end": 48.753,
          "en": "and I'll use signals here, but that of course is optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 55.73,
          "en": "Then I'll also add a method on toggle details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.86,
          "end": 60.483,
          "en": "where I wanna switch from false to true and vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "And there are now two ways of doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 66.96,
          "en": "Of course, since I'm using a signal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 69.9,
          "en": "I can't just set it to a new value like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 71.97,
          "en": "with an equal sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.97,
          "end": 74.64,
          "en": "Instead, you learned that you can use the set method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.64,
          "end": 76.443,
          "en": "to set a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 80.31,
          "en": "and here the new value should be the opposite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.31,
          "end": 82.28,
          "en": "of the old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.28,
          "end": 87.28,
          "en": "So we could read details visible like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "and as you learned, this won't set up a subscription here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 94.47,
          "en": "It would only do that inside of the effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.47,
          "end": 96.18299999999999,
          "en": "or inside of the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 99.87,
          "en": "But here we can read it once like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.87,
          "end": 101.55,
          "en": "Whenever this method is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.55,
          "end": 105.45,
          "en": "and to set details visible to the opposite of what it was,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.45,
          "end": 107.28,
          "en": "we can add an exclamation mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.28,
          "end": 109.593,
          "en": "in front of this details visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "So that way we'll set it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "to false if it was true and vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 118.413,
          "en": "That's one way of updating this signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.72999999999999,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "An alternative way, which I haven't covered yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 126.963,
          "en": "is that you call the update method on this Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.92,
          "end": 130.47,
          "en": "This method works almost like set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.47,
          "end": 135.243,
          "en": "but unlike set, it expects to get a function as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 140.55,
          "en": "and that function will be executed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.55,
          "end": 145.23,
          "en": "and Angular will automatically pass the old Signal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.23,
          "end": 148.23,
          "en": "as an argument to that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 150.15,
          "en": "So I'll name it was visible here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.15,
          "end": 151.6,
          "en": "though the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.91,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "And this function then needs to return the new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 158.172,
          "en": "to which the Signal should be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.172,
          "end": 162.06,
          "en": "So in my case, whatever was visible was not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.06,
          "end": 164.973,
          "en": "by adding an exclamation mark at the beginning here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 171.15,
          "en": "That way if we had true, we'll set false as a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.15,
          "end": 172.71,
          "en": "for details visible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.71,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "or if we had false, we'll set true as a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.24,
          "end": 180.54,
          "en": "And that's an alternative way of updating this signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.54,
          "end": 184.02,
          "en": "And it's up to you which approach you prefer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.02,
          "end": 188.13,
          "en": "With that, we got that details visible signal here though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.13,
          "end": 190.35,
          "en": "and they offer in that ticket component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.35,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "we can now use that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 195.81,
          "en": "to change the way different things are displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.81,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "in that template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 200.25,
          "en": "To be precise here for this if statement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.25,
          "end": 204.69,
          "en": "I now want to check if details visible is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.69,
          "end": 206.22,
          "en": "We could do it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.22,
          "end": 207.93,
          "en": "but since we're using JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.93,
          "end": 210.78,
          "en": "we can also just do it like this, rate the value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.78,
          "end": 212.4,
          "en": "and if that yields true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.4,
          "end": 214.713,
          "en": "that is all we need for this condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.39,
          "end": 218.85,
          "en": "Alternatively, we have this Ls case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.85,
          "end": 223.05,
          "en": "as you already learned before, or as you already saw before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.05,
          "end": 225.54,
          "en": "But then I also have this if check down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.54,
          "end": 228.933,
          "en": "where I also wanna check if details visible is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.82999999999998,
          "end": 231.06,
          "en": "because I only wanna show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.06,
          "end": 234.66,
          "en": "that ticket text here if the details are visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 234.66,
          "end": 237.603,
          "en": "So if I am expanding that ticket,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.55,
          "end": 241.2,
          "en": "and of course we must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.2,
          "end": 244.26,
          "en": "that on toggle details now gets called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.26,
          "end": 246.933,
          "en": "when the user does click some button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.07,
          "end": 249.93,
          "en": "So back in a ticket component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.93,
          "end": 252.307,
          "en": "here on that button at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.307,
          "end": 255.94,
          "en": "we should add the click event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.86,
          "end": 260.433,
          "en": "and trigger on toggle details like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 262.86,
          "end": 264.99,
          "en": "Well, and with that, if we save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.99,
          "end": 269.99,
          "en": "and we enter some ticket, you see it's not expanded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 270.15,
          "end": 273.213,
          "en": "by default, but if I click this, it does expand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.25,
          "end": 277.53,
          "en": "So that's now working the way it should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.53,
          "end": 278.76,
          "en": "with help of signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.76,
          "end": 280.95,
          "en": "But as mentioned before, you could of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.95,
          "end": 283.56,
          "en": "also implement the same functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.56,
          "end": 287.22,
          "en": "totally without signals, as you saw many times before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.22,
          "end": 288.633,
          "en": "in this course already.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
